    `Father, I go into the room today. I close the door. I pray to You who are unseen — and I receive that Your seeing of what is done in secret is itself the reward, before any specific outcome has been produced, before any prayer has been answered in the way I am asking. You see me here. In this room. In this moment. Before I have found the right words. The seeing is already happening. Let the secret place be the primary address of my spiritual life — not the performance of public religion, not the impression management that replaces genuine encounter, but the closed-door, unwitnessed, unhurried conversation with the Father who already knows what I need before I ask. Let what happens in this room today produce the fruit that appears in the rest of my day. And let the hiddenness of my life with Christ in God be the security from which I face everything that is not hidden. I am here. The door is closed. Speak.`
